Lunacy's System Alerts.

A hidden, headless app that opens webOS SystemUI's popup alerts when the system needs one: first,
the location service's question, "Allow the following application to use your location for
this session?" (LocationService.kt). It does what luna-systemui's SystemManagerService did when a
service asked, opening its alert page with the same window name, parameters and height.

The app's code is Lunacy's, under the same terms as the rest of Lunacy. The alert itself is
SystemUI's, which Lunacy serves at its webOS path from AndroidLuna/src/main/assets/luna-systemui
(SystemManagerAlerts/, stylesheets/ and images/): Palm's files from the reference TouchPad's
/usr/lib/luna/system/luna-systemui (webOS CE 3.1.0), copied unchanged on 2026-11-07,
abandonware like the rest of that folder (see its FilePicker NOTICE).

It also announces a new Lunacy release found by the daily update check (UpdateService.kt) as
SystemUI announced a waiting system update: a banner and an "Update available" dashboard with
the version, which opens System Updates. Its icons are SystemUI's notification-small-update.png
and notification-large-update.png, served from the same folder.
